From 40cb8aa1b80ae93a17ba41c126504ac65ba202be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:07:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] docs: document outbox events, the audit API and their
 configuration

Resource writes now produce outbox events that the application
publishes, and API writes produce audit records that tenants can list,
so operators need to know what is stored, how it is delivered and how
to recover it.

The CHANGELOG lists the new behaviour, the breaking changes to the
Outbox Python API and the fixed defects. The README documents the three
FORGEMESH_EVENT_WEBHOOK_* variables and how events and audit records
behave at runtime. The module mapping adds events.py, publishers.py and
version.py and the new test files, and moves audit records and outbox
events into the registry database. The backup runbook lists the two new
tables, explains what a restore means for events and audit records, and
shows how to list and redrive dead events.
---
